The table structure information is ({database name: {schema name: [table name]}}): 
{'IDC': {'IDC_V17': ['DICOM_METADATA']}}
Begin Exploring Related Columns
Below are the columns that appear to be central for finding “Embedding medium” and “Staining substance” information for slides (Modality = ‘SM’) together with the way each column (or JSON sub‑field) can be used:

• "Modality": modality filter – keep only slide‐microscopy (“SM”) instances  
• "SpecimenPreparationSequence": VARIANT that contains one or more preparation‑step objects  
    – inside every element there is usually "SpecimenPreparationStepContentItemSequence" which again is an array of content‑items  
    – every content‑item has  
        • "ConceptNameCodeSequence"[0]."CodeMeaning"   → tells us what the item describes (“Embedding medium”, “Staining substance”, …)  
        • "ConceptCodeSequence"[0]."CodeMeaning"       → actual value (“Paraffin wax”, “Hematoxylin”, …)  
        • "ConceptCodeSequence"[0]."CodingSchemeDesignator" (needs to equal ‘SCT’ for SNOMED CT codes)  
• "SOPInstanceUID": unique identifier that lets us associate several content‑items that belong to the same image

Typical conditions we will need  
    WHERE "Modality" = 'SM'  
    AND <ConceptName> ILIKE '%embedding%medium%'  (or   ILIKE '%staining%substance%')  
